Version 1.1.0. Everything that changed since 1.0.6.

[b]Competing Exchanges[/b]
[list]
[*]Your Exchange contests other Exchanges. You get one contest slot, plus one per Standing above Provincial, up to four. The slots sit at the top of the Competition section.
[*]Start a contest from the Leading Exchanges list or by right-clicking a country on the map. Contesting needs at least Engaged interest in the strategic region of their capital, and you cannot contest an Exchange that is already contesting you. Contesting raises your involvement in that region.
[*]Contests are a tug of war settled every 5 years. A draw, a win, or a decisive win that also takes part of the loser's investment pool income for a year.
[*]Ending a contest early counts as losing it where the bar stands now. The other Exchange gains as if it had won.
[*]Five competitor actions: Bear Raid, Lure Their Capital, Press Campaign, Hold the Line and Shore Up. They scale with the size of both Exchanges.
[*]When a competitor acts against you, an event lets you answer in kind, shore up or keep calm.
[*]AI Exchanges pick contests they can win, act more as a contest nears its end, and sometimes cut their losses.
[/list]

[b]Exchange score and Trust[/b]
[list]
[*]The Exchange score and the four Standings now show as one block, each Standing card filling as your score climbs through it.
[*]Trust has its own bar with its four levels named above it. Hover a level to see what it does.
[*]The score grows more slowly with sheer size, so more great powers can compete. The top three Exchanges are World Centres.
[/list]

[b]Paths to Renown[/b]
[list]
[*]Three new paths: Futures Pit, Lender to Nations and Railway Mania.
[*]Every path now has a drawback that grows with your place.
[/list]

[b]Blue Chips[/b]
[list]
[*]A company at 70 or more prosperity for 12 months becomes a blue chip. Blue chips soften crashes, build trust, lower loan interest and pull contests your way.
[*]New events when a company becomes a blue chip or starts slipping, and a yearly Company of the Year.
[*]A Blue Chips strip in the Speculation tab shows what yours give you.
[/list]

[b]Interface and fixes[/b]
[list]
[*]Finance tabs are renamed Trading Floor, Speculation, Banking and Exchanges.
[*]Shorter tooltips in vanilla's style. Translations in all 10 languages.
[*]Fixed a Great Issue or its cooldown sometimes never ending after loading a save.
[*]Fixed revolutionary journal entries not being inherited correctly.
[/list]
